---
title: Thai Basil Chicken and Garlic Butter Noodles
description: Sheet-pan curry-spiced chicken and asparagus served over rice noodles tossed in a garlicky coconut butter sauce with fresh Thai basil.
course: main
cuisine: Thai-inspired
servings: 4
time required: 30 minutes
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
source: https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/basil-chicken-and-garlic-noodles/#wprm-recipe-container-163565
image: https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Thai-Basil-Chicken-and-Garlic-Butter-Noodles-1-scaled.jpg
tags:
  - chicken
  - noodles
  - thai
  - sheet-pan
  - weeknight
---

Preheat the oven to 450°F.

On a #baking sheet{}, mix the @chicken breasts{1%pound}(thinly sliced) with the @shallot{1}(sliced), @yellow curry powder{2%tbsp}, @black pepper{1-2%tsp}, and @chili flakes{}. Toss to coat, then add @ghee{2%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, and @honey{2%tsp}, and toss again. Arrange the chicken in an even layer. Arrange the @asparagus{1%bunch}(chopped) to the side of the chicken and toss with @ghee{1%tbsp}. Season with @salt and @pepper.

Bake for ~{15-20%minutes}, until the chicken is cooked. Then toss with the @Thai basil{1/2%cup}.

Meanwhile, make the noodles. Melt the @salted butter{3%tbsp} in a #skillet{} set over medium heat. Add the @garlic{4%cloves}(chopped) and a pinch of @chili flakes{}. Cook until the garlic begins to caramelize and turn light golden brown, ~{1-2%minutes}. Stir in the @coconut milk{1%cup} and cook for ~{3-5%minutes}, until warmed through. Season with @salt. Remove from the heat and toss the @rice noodles{8%oz} with the sauce.

To serve, divide the noodles among bowls and top with chicken and asparagus. Serve with additional @basil{}, @green onions{}(sliced), and @limes{}. Enjoy!
